// CraneStudio curated model catalog — PLAN.md §8.1.
//
// Every entry here has actually been launched: downloaded (or already
// present locally), started with `cranestudio __serve`, and exercised
// against a real request. Adding a model is meant to be a pure data change
// — no code — so keep new entries to this same standard before merging.
//
// Entries marked `PENDING LAUNCH CHECK` are the exception, and are marked so
// they can be found with one grep. For those, everything that can be checked
// without a GPU has been: the commit sha, the exact file names and their
// byte-exact sizes come from the HuggingFace API at that sha, and the
// architecture / context / dimensions come from the repo's own `config.json`
// (or, for GGUF, from the family the file belongs to). What is *not* yet
// verified is the one thing that needs the hardware: that crane-serve loads it
// and answers a request. Clear the marker as each one is launched.
//
// Two Crane facts shape which format an entry can use (both read out of
// `crane-serve/src/engine/model_factory.rs`, `create_backend`):
//
//   * `--quant` (ISQ) is rejected for every model type except `qwen3_5`, so
//     `supports.isq` is false everywhere else — it isn't a conservative guess,
//     it's a hard guard in Crane.
//   * only `qwen3_5`, `qwen4_exp`, `minicpm5`, `minicpmv4_6` (4.7, with its
//     `mmproj` beside it), `gemma4` and `hunyuan` have GGUF loaders at all
//     (`qwen4_exp` has nothing else), and of those only `qwen3_5`,
//     `qwen4_exp`, `minicpm5` and `minicpmv4_6` read the tokenizer embedded
//     in the GGUF. `qwen3`, `gemma4` and `hunyuan` demand a sibling
//     `tokenizer.json` that the published GGUF repos don't ship, so those
//     families are catalogued as safetensors instead of shipping an entry that
//     cannot load.
